From 19376af5e1d158b01dd79cbf4e9610319ef933c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: storm pair-spec <pair-spec@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:37:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(uniswap-v2): admit only worlds without reentrant
 state change to the pair

An open world may answer an external call with any post-world, and SolidCore adopts the
pair storage it carries, so the specification cannot hold in every open world. Admit now
requires that answers keep the pair storage (PairFramed); a result of the bytes that only
a wider world explains is reported as Unadmitted, never as meeting the specification.
---
